# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# EAS resolves the project root to the git repo root and applies that
# .gitignore, not mobile/.gitignore — so `/android`, which is ignored
# locally, was still being packed into the build archive. That made the
# upload 392 MB (1.4 GB of Gradle output) and cost ~3 minutes per build
# for files EAS regenerates from scratch anyway.
#
# This file REPLACES .gitignore for archive purposes, so it has to
# re-state the ordinary excludes too, not just the android one.

# Generated native projects — EAS runs prebuild itself (see app.json;
# there is no ios/ or android/ committed to the repo).
/android
/ios

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled from package-lock.json.
node_modules/
dist/
web-build/
.expo/
.kotlin/
.gradle/

# Local tooling and scratch
.claude/
scripts/check-device.sh
*.log
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Credentials must never leave this machine
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.env*.local

# OS noise
.DS_Store
